# rm-socat forward rules, one per line, comma separated:
#   name , local_port , remote_host , remote_port , proto , ip
#
#   name         unique id (letters/digits/-/_) — also used to hash this
#                rule into a batch, see batches.conf
#   local_port   port this box listens on
#   remote_host  domain or IP to forward to
#   remote_port  port on remote_host
#   proto        tcp | udp | both
#   ip           dual (default: one socket serves both IPv4 and IPv6) | 4 | 6
#
# After editing, run: ./manage.sh apply
#
# Example (commented out — copy the line below, then edit it):
# rmg1 , 1232 , rmg1.example.com , 1232 , tcp , dual
